KEEP-ONLY-OWNER-ACCOUNT

Requested 2026-10-03 by the owner: "Sıfırdan test edeceğiz."

The care-data purge earlier the same day kept every account, because keeping the user
is what was asked for. Twelve survived. Removing the smoke test's leftovers took out
exactly one, which is what showed the other eleven are not smoke accounts at all —
they are earlier manual registrations. The owner wants production to hold their own
account and nothing else.

What goes: every account whose normalised address does not hash to the owner's digest,
with their sessions, memberships, subscriptions and entitlements, and the households
left with no remaining member.

What stays: the owner's account, and any household they belong to.

The owner is identified by the SHA-256 digest of their upper-cased address rather than
by the address itself, because this repository is public. A wrong digest cannot cause
damage: it would match no account, and the first guard stops the transaction before a
row is deleted.

This file is the confirmation. Remove it once the cleanup has run; the run that sees it
gone reports that there is nothing to do and passes.
